From 9b74581129def912c2960af862ba86203e3d2b28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fei Zhang <zhangfei@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 09:38:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/riscv: add RVV HEVC weighted interpolation

Use RVV for the existing weighted qpel and epel DSP entry points. Keep
the C functions for width 4 and width 6 epel blocks, where vector setup
exceeds the useful work on the tested processor.

The horizontal and vertical filters use widening multiply-accumulate.
Two-dimensional interpolation stores the horizontal result in an
intermediate 16-bit buffer before the vertical pass.
---
 libavcodec/riscv/Makefile                    |   2 +
 libavcodec/riscv/h26x/h2656dsp.h             |  35 +++++
 libavcodec/riscv/h26x/hevcdsp_weighted.c     | 155 +++++++++++++++++++
 libavcodec/riscv/h26x/hevcdsp_weighted_rvv.S | 119 ++++++++++++++
 libavcodec/riscv/hevcdsp_init.c              |  29 ++++
 5 files changed, 340 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libavcodec/riscv/h26x/hevcdsp_weighted.c
 create mode 100644 libavcodec/riscv/h26x/hevcdsp_weighted_rvv.S

